1
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:04,830
Three hundred thousand years ago,
you wake up in the tall grass...

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:07,040
and right next to you, there's a car.

3
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:12,440
Shiny. Red. Four doors. The logo
on the front is covered in mud.

4
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,410
It will stay that way forever.

5
00:00:14,530 --> 00:00:19,400
And by the end of this video, the whole
planet will be built around this one car.

6
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:21,120
Even the ostriches.

7
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:23,990
But first... we have a few problems.

8
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:31,070
Problem number one: fuel. A full tank
gets you maybe six hundred kilometers.

9
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:34,800
After that, it's a very
heavy, very red rock.

10
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:41,060
Problem number two: roads. There are none.
Just rocks, rivers, termite mounds...

11
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:43,360
and the occasional angry rhino.

12
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:47,260
Problem number three: you have
never seen a steering wheel.

13
00:00:47,310 --> 00:00:49,910
You think it's a very round snake.

14
00:00:50,130 --> 00:00:53,640
Problem number four: one
flat tire, and it's over.

15
00:00:53,710 --> 00:00:56,780
Rubber tires won't exist for almost
three hundred thousand years.

16
00:00:56,830 --> 00:00:58,330
So... let's install an upgrade.

17
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:03,470
Version one point oh. A fuel tank that
never runs out. Tires that fix themselves.

18
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:09,300
And in the glove box... the owner's manual.
Four hundred pages. Mostly pictures.

19
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:14,610
That's it. No roads. No GPS.
No driving license. And no,

20
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:17,170
it can't fly. Yet.

21
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:21,170
Oh, and no. There are no
dinosaurs. We'll get to that.

22
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:26,290
Day one. Your tribe, about thirty
people, gathers around the shiny beast.

23
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:29,860
The chief decides it's hungry.
He offers it a gazelle leg.

24
00:01:30,610 --> 00:01:32,840
The car does not eat the gazelle leg.

25
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:34,980
You climb inside. You touch everything.

26
00:01:35,030 --> 00:01:38,400
Then you press the middle
of the round snake.

27
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:39,990
HONK.

28
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:44,290
Thirty people are in a tree in under
two seconds. Including the chief.

29
00:01:44,390 --> 00:01:46,360
Including the chief's grandmother.

30
00:01:46,870 --> 00:01:52,390
Day two: the first drive in human history.
You turn the key, the engine roars,

31
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:57,840
and you move forward... at three kilometers
an hour. The tribe walks next to you.

32
00:01:57,940 --> 00:01:59,220
Some of them are faster.

33
00:01:59,350 --> 00:02:01,050
Then you find the other pedal.

34
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:06,040
Sixty kilometers an hour. Your
hair flies back. The tribe screams.

35
00:02:06,090 --> 00:02:09,360
They think the beast is eating
you. Ninety seconds later,

36
00:02:09,410 --> 00:02:13,180
you have the first car
accident in human history.

37
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:15,890
You hit the only tree for ten kilometers.

38
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:18,910
The same tree the whole tribe
was hiding in yesterday.

39
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:24,640
Day five. Something is running next to
your window. Long legs. Big eyes. Feathers.

40
00:02:24,690 --> 00:02:25,670
An ostrich.

41
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:31,340
You speed up. It speeds up.
Sixty. Sixty-five. Seventy.

42
00:02:31,390 --> 00:02:36,170
The first race in history: a car
against a dinosaur. Technically.

43
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:39,210
You hit a termite mound. The ostrich wins.

44
00:02:39,350 --> 00:02:41,410
This one's real, by the way.

45
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:43,870
Ostriches can sprint at about
seventy kilometers an hour.

46
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:45,920
They're the fastest birds on land.

47
00:02:46,510 --> 00:02:51,910
Week two: hunting by car. Gazelles
are fast, but they can't outrun a car.

48
00:02:51,990 --> 00:02:56,350
They can, however, turn.
Cars can't turn like that.

49
00:02:56,450 --> 00:03:01,390
But the car is great at one thing: carrying
home everything you hunt. In the trunk.

50
00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:06,550
The downside? The engine is loud. The
herds learn to run the moment they hear it.

51
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:10,420
Soon the hunters have to walk twice
as far to find anything at all.

52
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:15,670
Week three: the car becomes a
house. Five seats. Thirty people.

53
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:20,720
Every night is a fight for the back seat.
But on cold nights, there's the heater.

54
00:03:20,770 --> 00:03:22,390
Nobody freezes anymore.

55
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:25,810
And the cup holder? The
tribe has never seen a cup.

56
00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:28,750
They stare at the little
round hole for days.

57
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:33,300
Then your cousin carves one out of
wood. The first cup in human history.

58
00:03:33,350 --> 00:03:34,950
Invented to fit a car.

59
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:40,910
Month two. You open the glove box and find
the manual. You can't read a single word.

60
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:45,910
But you can read the pictures. A
wheel. An axle. A wheel on an axle.

61
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:49,490
Your cousin builds a copy out of
wood. The first one is square.

62
00:03:49,590 --> 00:03:52,110
The second one is round. The wheel.

63
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:55,300
Invented almost three
hundred thousand years early.

64
00:03:55,350 --> 00:04:00,740
In your world, the oldest wooden wheel ever
found is about five thousand years old.

65
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:06,540
Month four: the first road trip. The next
tribe lives a hundred kilometers away.

66
00:04:06,590 --> 00:04:13,190
On foot, that's four days. By car? Two
hours. They meet you, and they run up a tree.

67
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:18,610
But this time, you bring gifts.
Meat. Cups. One very loud honk.

68
00:04:18,710 --> 00:04:22,820
By evening, the two tribes are
trading. Stone tools for berries.

69
00:04:22,870 --> 00:04:26,180
Fire tricks for fishing
tricks. For the first time,

70
00:04:26,230 --> 00:04:28,930
the people over the hill aren't strangers.

71
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:35,350
Year one. Thirty-four people. Distance
driven: forty thousand kilometers. Trees hit:

72
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:40,080
three. Races against the
ostrich: twelve. Races won: zero.

73
00:04:40,130 --> 00:04:44,830
And you are now officially... "The
One Who Rides the Roaring Beast."

74
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:46,600
Okay. Let's speed this up.

75
00:04:46,690 --> 00:04:51,940
Year ten. Everyone wants a car. There's
only one. So the tribe builds copies:

76
00:04:51,990 --> 00:04:56,370
a wooden box on four round wheels.
No engine. Somebody has to pull it.

77
00:04:56,450 --> 00:05:01,820
At first, people pull. Then someone
has a terrible idea. The ostrich.

78
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:06,180
Two ostriches on a rope, one wooden
cart, and a very brave passenger.

79
00:05:06,230 --> 00:05:10,090
The first dinosaur-powered
vehicle in history. Technically.

80
00:05:10,290 --> 00:05:15,250
Year fifty. The tracks the carts leave
become paths. The paths become roads.

81
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:20,060
And on the very first road...
the very first traffic jam.

82
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:23,170
Forty ostrich carts and
one confused mammoth.

83
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:27,920
The good part? Roads connect everything.
Tribes trade, travel, marry each other.

84
00:05:27,970 --> 00:05:32,500
Words, songs and ideas move
faster than ever. The bad part?

85
00:05:32,550 --> 00:05:36,060
Roads cut straight through the
land. Herds stop crossing them.

86
00:05:36,110 --> 00:05:37,740
Some valleys go quiet.

87
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,670
Year one hundred. Too many
carts. Too many crashes.

88
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:46,680
So the elders invent the first traffic
rule: the big red car always goes first.

89
00:05:46,730 --> 00:05:49,690
Then they invent the first
traffic light: a man named Ug,

90
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:51,990
holding a red stone and a green leaf.

91
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:55,940
In your world, the first traffic light
went up in London in eighteen sixty-eight.

92
00:05:55,990 --> 00:06:00,860
It ran on gas... and a few weeks
later, it exploded. Ug never exploded.

93
00:06:00,910 --> 00:06:02,450
Ug is very proud of that.

94
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:07,970
Year two hundred: the first speeding ticket.
It's carved on a forty-kilo stone slab.

95
00:06:08,020 --> 00:06:11,930
You have to carry it home
yourself. The fine: one gazelle.

96
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:12,690
In your world,

97
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:17,260
the first speeding fine went to a man in
England in eighteen ninety-six. His speed?

98
00:06:17,310 --> 00:06:20,400
Thirteen kilometers an
hour. Four times the limit.

99
00:06:20,610 --> 00:06:24,330
Year one thousand. The First
Car now sits in a temple.

100
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:27,010
The engine has been running
for a thousand years,

101
00:06:27,060 --> 00:06:31,020
because nobody knows how to turn it
off. The honk is used as a prayer bell.

102
00:06:31,070 --> 00:06:35,260
And kids learn to read from the manual.
The first sentence everybody can read:

103
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:37,270
"Check tire pressure every month."

104
00:06:37,510 --> 00:06:40,820
Year three thousand. To copy
the engine, you need metal.

105
00:06:40,870 --> 00:06:44,260
So people learn to melt rocks:
copper, then bronze, then iron.

106
00:06:44,310 --> 00:06:49,790
And they go looking for the black water
that smells like the car. They find it. Oil.

107
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:52,510
And with oil come the first oil wars.

108
00:06:52,670 --> 00:06:58,300
Year five thousand. The first real car
built by human hands. Wood. Bronze.

109
00:06:58,350 --> 00:07:03,600
A steam engine. Top speed: eight kilometers
an hour. The ostrich is not impressed.

110
00:07:03,650 --> 00:07:07,960
In your world, the first real car came
from Karl Benz in eighteen eighty-six.

111
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:12,730
And the first long road trip? His wife,
Bertha. She took the car without asking,

112
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:16,920
drove over a hundred kilometers...
and bought fuel at a pharmacy.

113
00:07:16,970 --> 00:07:20,980
That pharmacy is called the
first gas station in history.

114
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:27,220
Year six thousand. Car companies!
Mammoth Motors. Rockswagen. Fer-rock-i.

115
00:07:27,270 --> 00:07:32,720
Ostrich Martin. And the strangest
cars ever built. A car with legs,

116
00:07:32,770 --> 00:07:37,110
for places without roads. A car
that swims. A convertible...

117
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:40,520
which was just a normal car,
until a mammoth sat on it.

118
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:45,760
Year ten thousand. One car for every
family. And the price shows up.

119
00:07:45,810 --> 00:07:50,150
Traffic jams that last three
days. Smoke over every valley.

120
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:54,770
Kids can't play in the street anymore.
And crashes. Even in your world,

121
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:58,390
roads take about one point
two million lives every year.

122
00:07:58,450 --> 00:08:03,810
Here, they did one thing early. On page
one of the manual, there was a picture:

123
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:08,400
a person, a belt, a click. They read
it three hundred thousand years early.

124
00:08:08,450 --> 00:08:09,930
Everybody buckles up.

125
00:08:09,990 --> 00:08:13,450
Still, the good side is huge. Ambulances.

126
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:15,900
Food trucks that reach
villages during droughts.

127
00:08:15,950 --> 00:08:18,780
Cities that trade across whole continents.

128
00:08:18,930 --> 00:08:23,070
Year twenty thousand. The traffic
jam has lasted three days again.

129
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:28,610
Somebody looks up and says the words
that change everything: "What if... up?"

130
00:08:28,750 --> 00:08:30,950
Flying cars. In your world,

131
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,730
people have been promising flying
cars for about a hundred years. Here,

132
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:40,360
they just built them. Two weeks later:
the first traffic jam in the sky.

133
00:08:40,410 --> 00:08:42,400
The birds are furious.

134
00:08:42,570 --> 00:08:46,190
Year one hundred thousand.
Cars drive themselves.

135
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:49,770
A highway goes all the way around
the planet. And the First Car?

136
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:54,120
It's in a museum now. Engine still
running. Odometer stuck at nine million,

137
00:08:54,170 --> 00:08:58,800
nine hundred ninety-nine thousand, nine
hundred ninety-nine. The mud on the logo?

138
00:08:58,850 --> 00:08:59,810
Still there.

139
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:04,410
So, fast forward to today. Two
thousand twenty-six. Except here,

140
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:08,740
they call it the year three
hundred thousand, A.V. After Vroom.

141
00:09:08,870 --> 00:09:10,580
Here's what's different from your world.

142
00:09:10,810 --> 00:09:15,270
One. People here have been driving for
almost three hundred thousand years.

143
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:17,730
You've been driving for
about one hundred and forty.

144
00:09:17,940 --> 00:09:22,980
Two. Every city on Earth is built
around one road: the Old Ostrich Road.

145
00:09:23,030 --> 00:09:26,030
The first road ever.
It's a holiday route now.

146
00:09:26,280 --> 00:09:30,740
Three. The biggest sport on the planet
isn't football. It's ostrich racing.

147
00:09:30,790 --> 00:09:34,180
And the ostrich still beats
most cars off the line.

148
00:09:34,410 --> 00:09:39,600
Four. Mammoths never went extinct. They
pulled carts for fifty thousand years.

149
00:09:39,650 --> 00:09:43,860
Then cars took their jobs. Now they're
retired, in giant nature parks.

150
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:44,830
Five.

151
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:49,650
Every car on Earth still has a cup holder
in exactly the same place as the First Car.

152
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:52,010
Nobody remembers why. Tradition.

153
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:58,330
Six. The word for "hello" is a honk.
A short one. A long honk is very rude.

154
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:01,690
Seven. The longest traffic jam in
history lasted forty-one years.

155
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:04,460
People were born in it.
People got married in it.

156
00:10:04,510 --> 00:10:08,210
Somebody wrote a whole
book about it. In it.

157
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:12,590
Eight. Wheels are so old that nobody
thinks of them as an invention.

158
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:17,280
Asking "who invented the wheel?" here
is like asking "who invented walking?"

159
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:21,050
Nine. Speaking of walking:
it's an extreme sport now.

160
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:24,230
Walking ten kilometers
gets you on the news.

161
00:10:24,510 --> 00:10:29,420
Ten. Nobody calls it a steering wheel.
Everyone still calls it the round snake.

162
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:33,910
Not everything is better, though. A
third of the land is covered by roads.

163
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:36,940
Wild animals live in
special "road-free zones."

164
00:10:36,990 --> 00:10:40,400
And the air in some cities still
smells like the black water.

165
00:10:40,650 --> 00:10:42,610
And maybe the biggest difference of all:

166
00:10:42,660 --> 00:10:45,690
the first thing the car
taught humanity wasn't speed.

167
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:49,650
It was that the people over the hill
weren't monsters. They were neighbors.

168
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:52,780
Back on day one, before
the tribe went to sleep,

169
00:10:52,830 --> 00:10:55,730
the chief left one more
gazelle leg next to the car.

170
00:10:55,830 --> 00:10:57,810
Just in case it got hungry in the night.

171
00:10:58,050 --> 00:11:02,590
Three hundred thousand years later,
it's still there. In the museum.

172
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:03,990
Right next to the tire.

173
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:08,970
And the dinosaurs? Still none. Except
the ostrich. Which, in this timeline,

174
00:11:09,020 --> 00:11:12,170
has never lost a race. Not one.

175
00:11:12,270 --> 00:11:13,950
So here's my question for you:

176
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,530
if you woke up three hundred
thousand years ago next to a car,

177
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:20,290
where would you drive first?
Tell me in the comments.

178
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:23,040
The best answer might end
up in a future episode.

179
00:11:23,090 --> 00:11:28,680
Next time: you get a game console. No
electricity. No TV. Twenty-nine people.

180
00:11:28,730 --> 00:11:32,630
One controller. Subscribe, so
you don't miss the next upgrade.

